{"key":"39c3d838af96502e6613479b2eed382d257de9fd6fb687b8ae4ef47b2ec19399","quote":"Split the work and save partial results","text":"The instruction \"Split the work and save partial results\" is the Do cell for the Timeout row, and the cause there says the script ran past five minutes. The instruction itself sets no number; it points at the table row, which gives the five-minute threshold. The task asks whether the instruction states or points at a table that gives a number limiting it. The Timeout row's cause gives \"five minutes,\" which is a duration that limits when this remedy applies. So the instruction does point at a table giving a limiting duration.\n\n{\"limits\": [{\"limit\": 5, \"comparison\": \"gt\", \"unit\": \"minutes\"}]}","usage":{"input":498,"output":191}}
